WEBVTT

01:04.480 --> 01:05.850
Take a look at this.

01:07.520 --> 01:13.110
This is where we think the mysterious incidents
related to the mutant phenomenon occurred.

01:13.780 --> 01:15.530
I circled the area.

01:16.200 --> 01:20.080
At the center is
a remote mountainous region.

01:20.080 --> 01:22.700
This is where the cause of
the mutant detection interference

01:22.700 --> 01:25.420
and the secondary mutations
are to be found?

01:25.790 --> 01:26.960
Yes.

01:26.960 --> 01:28.380
Prioritize this when
you investigate.

01:31.420 --> 01:35.510
<i>Yes, they are heading
here once again.</i>

01:35.510 --> 01:37.550
<i>But rest assured.</i>

01:37.550 --> 01:39.390
<i>This time, I'll definitely...</i>

01:40.140 --> 01:44.520
Just in case,
I've called our comrades here.

01:44.520 --> 01:49.230
I'm expecting you to
finish off the X-Men.

01:49.230 --> 01:50.360
<i>Leave it to me.</i>

01:52.530 --> 01:56.530
<i>The real fight begins now, Professor X.</i>

01:56.530 --> 02:00.120
<i>I can imagine the look of surprise
on your face.</i>

02:03.490 --> 02:10.000
<b><i>Conflict - Fierce Fight</i></b>

02:17.050 --> 02:18.180
We've been waiting for you.

02:21.550 --> 02:22.720
Hisako!

02:22.720 --> 02:24.060
You look cool!

02:24.060 --> 02:25.270
Right?!

02:28.390 --> 02:29.190
Welcome home.

02:29.770 --> 02:31.610
It looks good on you.

02:31.610 --> 02:32.610
I'm home!

02:32.610 --> 02:36.240
Really, it's as if you've
grown up all of a sudden.

02:36.240 --> 02:37.900
Like you're a different person!

02:37.900 --> 02:39.030
Thank you, Emma.

02:39.030 --> 02:40.110
It's all thanks to you.

02:40.740 --> 02:43.700
For selecting her as
a member of the X-Men,

02:43.700 --> 02:45.040
even though she's a trainee.

02:45.540 --> 02:48.120
I just stayed close and
watched over her.

02:48.670 --> 02:54.130
It's was all Cyclops' and Wolverine's
strict training that strengthened her.

02:54.670 --> 02:58.970
Our training was a bit rough,
but Hisako toughed it out.

02:59.380 --> 03:02.970
And believe me, we've only scratched
the surface of your daughter's potential.

03:03.600 --> 03:05.770
With more experience,
she will become stronger.

03:05.770 --> 03:10.850
She's learning what it means to be an X-Man,
and she's grown as a person as well.

03:10.850 --> 03:12.520
She has a very bright future.

03:12.980 --> 03:14.480
I see.

03:14.480 --> 03:16.440
Good for you, Hisako.

03:18.150 --> 03:22.910
I'm still inexperienced, and there're
plenty of things I have to learn,

03:22.910 --> 03:28.330
but I'll do my best as an X-Man who bridges
humans and mutants together!

03:32.170 --> 03:34.710
Everyone, you must be tired
from the long trip,

03:34.710 --> 03:37.510
but people hoping to receive
the vaccine have gathered, so...

03:38.210 --> 03:40.720
By all means, let's get started.

03:40.720 --> 03:41.760
Thank you.

03:42.760 --> 03:44.140
And, also...

03:44.890 --> 03:45.600
What is it?

03:46.180 --> 03:51.140
Actually, it's about something that happened
while you were in New York.

03:51.980 --> 03:56.650
There are lots of dead fish floating
in the nearby town's river...

03:56.650 --> 04:01.650
the trees are deforming;
strange things happening.

04:02.200 --> 04:06.080
And a railway bridge deep in the mountains
was twisted and deformed!

04:06.830 --> 04:12.080
People here are getting scared
and think that mutants did these things.

04:13.500 --> 04:14.790
I understand.

04:14.790 --> 04:15.920
We'll look into it.

04:17.960 --> 04:20.210
Beast, I leave the vaccine to you.

04:20.210 --> 04:21.340
Okay.

04:21.340 --> 04:23.010
Wolverine and Storm
will head to the river.

04:23.840 --> 04:25.550
We'll head to the railway bridge.

04:38.940 --> 04:41.570
It should mitigate
the symptoms you've been having.

04:41.570 --> 04:42.950
Thank you.

04:45.280 --> 04:46.950
But really...

04:52.710 --> 04:57.710
To think that the Professor
couldn't detect mutants

04:57.710 --> 05:00.800
with Cerebro when there's
so many of them here...

05:00.800 --> 05:02.420
Next, please!

05:05.510 --> 05:06.390
Um...

05:07.850 --> 05:10.850
My arms changed into this...

05:11.220 --> 05:12.810
Secondary mutation?

05:13.310 --> 05:16.400
Um, will the vaccine
still work despite that?

05:17.440 --> 05:20.110
At the very least,
it won't get any worse.

05:20.110 --> 05:23.360
When did it get like that?

05:24.860 --> 05:26.320
I see.

05:26.320 --> 05:29.910
Three months ago,
this happened suddenly?

05:29.910 --> 05:30.410
Yes.

05:38.710 --> 05:40.920
The river flow seems normal...

05:41.670 --> 05:43.510
I smell decay from upstream...

05:45.930 --> 05:47.680
but this smell isn't just that.

05:48.970 --> 05:50.510
This scent...!

05:53.470 --> 05:55.690
What's with the river's color?!

05:57.810 --> 05:58.480
I don't know.

05:59.110 --> 06:01.650
But it sure ain't anything good.

06:18.460 --> 06:19.290
Yuck!

06:19.830 --> 06:22.340
Makes me wish I didn't have
these heightened senses!

06:22.750 --> 06:26.220
What's with this huge
amount of gas?!

06:29.760 --> 06:34.390
With the bridge in a state like this,
it must be the work of a mutant, right?

06:34.390 --> 06:36.680
I guess we have no choice
but to make that assumption.

06:37.890 --> 06:41.610
Only Magneto is capable
of something like this.

06:41.610 --> 06:46.110
But he's locked away in prison,
so it couldn't be him.

06:47.700 --> 06:51.660
In any case,
it's worse than we heard.

06:58.790 --> 07:00.630
Hey, Cyclops.

07:00.630 --> 07:05.760
Beast said that your heart
was deeply wounded.

07:06.420 --> 07:09.180
That it was a wound that
wouldn't easily disappear.

07:09.180 --> 07:10.640
What happened?

07:12.890 --> 07:14.560
Please stop, Hisako.

07:15.060 --> 07:18.020
You mustn't lightly tread
into someone's heart.

07:40.160 --> 07:42.210
Depending on their ability,

07:42.210 --> 07:44.880
some mutants may be capable of
doing that to the bridge...

07:45.750 --> 07:49.470
But we cannot conclude
that a mutant is responsible.

07:50.050 --> 07:51.800
The same thing goes for
the gas fields.

07:52.510 --> 07:56.930
In any case, something is happening
without our knowledge.

07:57.640 --> 08:00.980
What's more, people think mutants
have done this.

08:03.810 --> 08:05.190
I finally finished.

08:05.770 --> 08:08.030
Kyouko really helped me out.

08:08.030 --> 08:08.900
Thank you.

08:08.900 --> 08:10.400
You're welcome.

08:10.990 --> 08:13.530
Hisako, I thank you as well for
helping with the cleanup.

08:14.490 --> 08:17.080
Now, it's time to
help out with dinner.

08:17.080 --> 08:19.370
- Come on, Kyoko!
- Don't push me!

08:19.830 --> 08:22.370
I'm glad there was somehow
enough vaccine.

08:22.370 --> 08:25.460
I vaccinated the mutants with signs
of secondary mutations first.

08:26.090 --> 08:27.550
To think there'd be that many.

08:28.250 --> 08:32.170
And among them there were those already
undergoing secondary mutation.

08:32.720 --> 08:38.310
And surprisingly, they all lived within
this circular region where

08:38.310 --> 08:40.350
the mutant phenomenon
is manifesting.

08:41.600 --> 08:45.940
And everyone there has undergone secondary
mutation in the past few years.

08:45.940 --> 08:49.530
Which means that at
the center of this circle,

08:50.190 --> 08:53.900
we've got the cause of
the secondary mutations.

08:54.360 --> 08:56.410
Probably so.

08:56.410 --> 08:57.410
All right, then.

08:57.410 --> 08:58.950
We'll check tomorrow morning.

09:29.860 --> 09:32.190
We've entered the center
of the circle.

09:36.490 --> 09:38.160
What's wrong, Emma?

09:38.660 --> 09:40.160
A strange noise...

09:40.950 --> 09:42.450
my head hurts!

09:42.790 --> 09:43.870
Noise?

09:44.330 --> 09:45.960
I can't hear anything.

09:52.880 --> 09:54.050
Hey Cyclops!

09:54.050 --> 09:54.970
What's going on?!

09:54.970 --> 09:56.550
I can't control the craft!

09:57.720 --> 09:58.930
Do something!

10:03.020 --> 10:05.060
A missile is approaching rapidly!

10:06.850 --> 10:07.770
It's no good!

10:07.770 --> 10:08.560
I can't dodge it!

10:09.230 --> 10:10.610
Brace for impact!

10:29.170 --> 10:30.500
How's Emma?

10:30.500 --> 10:32.750
Her headache's gotten worse.

10:33.380 --> 10:37.170
Once we entered the center,
abnormal events began to occur.

10:37.170 --> 10:39.340
It seems they're correlated.

10:39.890 --> 10:40.760
Dammit!

10:40.760 --> 10:41.890
What's going on?

10:43.970 --> 10:45.600
What's that noise?

10:48.730 --> 10:51.480
Is that what you
heard earlier, Emma?

10:51.480 --> 10:52.520
Those weird noises?

10:55.030 --> 10:55.610
Emma!

11:02.490 --> 11:03.620
<i>What's that?!</i>

11:04.580 --> 11:06.700
<i>What happened to the X-men!</i>

11:22.430 --> 11:24.010
Hey, Storm!

11:24.680 --> 11:26.640
Do something with your powers!

11:26.640 --> 11:27.890
Don't ask the impossible.

11:28.680 --> 11:31.190
This isn't weather related.

11:44.450 --> 11:46.160
Emma, are you alright?

11:47.120 --> 11:48.120
It stopped.

11:48.700 --> 11:53.040
There's definitely somethin' big
going on around here.

11:53.040 --> 11:58.130
It may be some kind of power
that causes secondary mutations.

11:58.800 --> 12:01.720
In any case, it's dangerous to
return to the Blackbird.

12:02.300 --> 12:03.680
It may explode.

12:04.300 --> 12:05.470
Let's move away from here.

12:27.740 --> 12:29.080
U-Men leftovers?

12:47.720 --> 12:49.140
I'll be your opponent.

12:52.100 --> 12:52.600
Everyone!

12:52.890 --> 12:53.810
Get back!

13:08.660 --> 13:10.950
Not bad, visor punk.

13:12.250 --> 13:13.120
Take this!

13:30.220 --> 13:31.640
Cyclops!

13:31.640 --> 13:32.770
You bastard!

13:35.310 --> 13:38.860
Next is the loudmouth with
the metal-reinforced skeleton.

13:46.490 --> 13:47.160
What?

13:56.540 --> 13:58.960
Melt with your adamantium!

14:02.710 --> 14:03.760
Wolverine!

14:03.760 --> 14:06.880
Weathergirl, play with this!

14:27.240 --> 14:29.160
Wolverine, I'm coming!

14:30.240 --> 14:31.200
Bastard!

14:35.370 --> 14:38.000
He should have
a weakness somewhere.

14:48.930 --> 14:49.430
Hisako!

14:49.680 --> 14:52.180
I don't have much data
on you two...

14:53.720 --> 14:55.060
but it seems I won't need any.

15:10.610 --> 15:12.160
I can't use telepathy!

15:18.540 --> 15:19.870
Why you...!

15:31.970 --> 15:32.800
Hisako!

15:37.810 --> 15:40.350
The shield emitter should
be on his spine.

15:40.690 --> 15:42.020
If I aim there...

15:53.950 --> 15:56.580
I have only one, but it's all yours.

16:34.410 --> 16:36.660
Everyone,
get away from there!

16:43.580 --> 16:44.420
He did it!

16:53.470 --> 16:55.220
You bastards...

16:55.760 --> 16:57.140
<i>I'll make you pay!</i>

17:17.410 --> 17:18.240
Are you okay?

17:18.240 --> 17:19.910
Yeah, somehow.

17:23.120 --> 17:25.170
Man, my shoulders are stiff.

17:34.880 --> 17:36.090
This is...

17:36.090 --> 17:37.890
a mutant detection system?

17:37.890 --> 17:38.970
What?!

17:38.970 --> 17:40.600
It's similar to Cerebro.

17:41.100 --> 17:44.520
To think someone besides us had
something like this...

17:45.140 --> 17:46.440
What does it mean?

17:47.020 --> 17:50.400
Even we couldn't detect
mutants in this area.

17:53.320 --> 17:55.700
There're monsters here.

17:55.700 --> 18:00.700
Far more dangerous
than you mutants.

18:03.580 --> 18:04.330
Watch out!

18:04.330 --> 18:05.790
Everyone, get away from here!

18:08.880 --> 18:11.920
No matter how you struggle,

18:11.920 --> 18:14.970
you can't do anything
against those monsters.

18:26.520 --> 18:29.940
To think the U-Men developed mutant detection
technology at the same time as us,

18:29.940 --> 18:32.070
and sought out mutants with it...

18:32.730 --> 18:36.190
Which means that the U-Men
weren't the ones interfering

18:36.190 --> 18:38.110
with the mutant detection.

18:38.610 --> 18:41.990
So, who the hell is?

19:13.940 --> 19:14.610
Hisako!

19:15.320 --> 19:16.110
Are you okay?

19:17.820 --> 19:19.740
Beast's back is warm!

19:23.330 --> 19:25.080
But you can't fall asleep.

19:25.700 --> 19:29.290
You can't see a Broadway musical
from the inside of a coffin.

19:29.290 --> 19:33.210
Yeah, last time we didn't make it.

19:36.000 --> 19:37.170
I smell someone.

19:40.180 --> 19:40.930
Over there!

20:03.320 --> 20:05.490
We're lost and in trouble.

20:05.490 --> 20:08.500
Please, can you let us stay here?

20:11.370 --> 20:12.120
Go ahead.

20:22.590 --> 20:23.930
Here's some tea.

20:23.930 --> 20:25.350
It'll warm you up.

20:30.270 --> 20:31.100
Thanks.

20:34.980 --> 20:36.480
U-um...

20:38.400 --> 20:40.740
Mrs. Sasaki Yui?

20:43.780 --> 20:44.910
<i>Sasaki...</i>

20:44.910 --> 20:45.870
<i>Yui?</i>

20:46.320 --> 20:49.330
That's right,
the Sasaki Institute!

20:49.330 --> 20:52.660
When Professor X asked me
about it back in New York,

20:52.660 --> 20:54.920
I couldn't really remember, but...

20:54.920 --> 20:57.000
you're Dr. Sasaki, aren't you?

20:57.540 --> 20:58.880
Y-Yes...

20:58.880 --> 21:01.130
I'm lchiki Hisako!

21:01.840 --> 21:02.720
Hisako?

21:02.720 --> 21:06.970
I can't believe I'd meet my teacher
in a place like this!

21:07.510 --> 21:12.140
I went to the Sasaki Institute
when I was little.

21:12.140 --> 21:14.900
It's an institution for the schooling
of mutant children,

21:14.900 --> 21:17.190
and the headmaster
was Mrs. Sasaki!

21:17.190 --> 21:20.070
I wonder why I didn't
remember it until now!

21:20.070 --> 21:21.030
That's so weird!

23:03.840 --> 23:06.720
The quiet institution in
the remote mountains.

23:06.720 --> 23:09.340
The woman the X-Men met there,

23:09.340 --> 23:10.390
Sasaki Yui.

23:11.430 --> 23:13.890
In her words and attitude,

23:13.890 --> 23:15.970
Emma senses a secret.

23:17.230 --> 23:20.150
At the same time,
Professor X, in New York,

23:20.150 --> 23:22.480
accepts a call from Sasaki Yui

23:22.480 --> 23:24.320
and is told the secret
about her education.

23:25.650 --> 23:31.070
<b><i>Betrayal - Shock</i></b>

23:25.780 --> 23:27.400
Next time, on X-Men:

23:28.240 --> 23:29.070
Shock.
